# NOTICE — provenance and third-party licenses

This repository is a driver-only extraction for the Xiaomi Mi 11 (`venus`)
iOS bring-up. It combines original work with the following third-party components.

## Base platform
- **XNU** (`xnu-8796.121.2`) — Apple Public Source License 2.0. See `LICENSE`.
- **hackios-xnu-kernel** platform layer (upstream:
  `https://github.com/oosexgang/hackios-xnu-kernel`) — APSL 2.0. The `redwood_*`
  and `venus_*` drivers here are original Mi 11 bring-up work layered on it.

## Wi-Fi (`wifi/`)
The Wi-Fi radio object `ath11k-vlmd.o` is built from:
- **Linux `ath11k`** (Qualcomm WCN6750/QCA6490 driver), from a pinned Linux
  release — **BSD-3-Clause-Clear** (the one `ath/` header it includes is ISC).
  The driver files are used unmodified.
- **FreeBSD LinuxKPI** headers (pinned FreeBSD release) — **BSD-2-Clause**,
  patched via `wifi/lx-vlmd/patches/*.patch`.
- **`wifi/lx-vlmd`** — original compatibility layer (headers + OS glue) written
  for this port, on top of the kernel's `redwood_lx` bus.

The `venus_lmd_*` kernel driver (MHI / QRTR / QMI / radio bring-up) is an
independent port of the lemonade (OnePlus 9) QCA6490 board driver from
`https://github.com/b1ackm4x/hackios-xnu-kernel`, adapted for the Mi 11.

## Touch (`touch/`)
- `redwood_focaltech_fw.h` is generated from the FocalTech touch-panel controller
  firmware (`focaltech_ts_fw_m20.bin`). It is vendor firmware required by the
  touch driver and contains no device identity.
- The ST FTS protocol implementation (`redwood_venus_st_protocol.c`,
  `redwood_st_touch.h`) was ported from ST's own FTS driver reference.

## Bluetooth / Audio / Display / Battery
Bluetooth is adapted from the lemonade reference in
`https://github.com/b1ackm4x/hackios-xnu-kernel`; audio, display and battery are
original Mi 11 bring-up work. Bluetooth uses the phone's own controller firmware
loaded at runtime (not included). Audio uses the CS35L41 amplifier and the SoC
ADSP; display uses the Adreno GPU and the DPU. No third-party source is bundled
for these beyond the XNU/IOKit base.

## Sanitization note
Compiled objects were stripped of debug information to remove build-host paths.
No credentials, device identifiers, or firmware/calibration blobs are included.